| `wget`                            | `curl`                                                       |
| --------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Mainly used to **download files** | Mainly used to **transfer data / communicate with servers**  |
| Very convenient for downloading   | More flexible for APIs, HTTP requests, etc.                  |
| Can recursively download websites | Doesn't focus on recursive downloading                       |
| Simple download syntax            | More options for HTTP methods, headers, authentication, etc. |

1. wget — downloading a file:----> 

   ex: wget https://example.com/file.zip ---->  This downloads file.zip to your current directory.

2. curl — communicating with a server

   ex: curl https://example.com  --->  It displays the response in your terminal.
